<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4a3a4f9f-dd4c-5721-a2c2-c197e1373ad1" activityNameId="7cfa459e-fdf4-550c-8448-fb4bc1adce5e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation system for appartment buildings, PE ducts, without GHE</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation system for appartment buildings, PE ducts, without GHE
Disposal of a ventilation system for an appartment building with a specific air flow rate of 0.92 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. The reference value of the inventory is 1 m2 heated gross floor area. The inventory is based on a study of an appartment building with 6 flats, a heated gross floor area of 780 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 720 m3/h. The inventory includes an average of decentral and central systems. It includes average components for air handling units, ducts (including 30mm thermal insulation where needed), air valves, roof-hoods, dampers and silencers. No insuation for fire protection or fire dampers included. The data represents horizontal ductwork mainly made of polyethylene and vertical ductwork mainly made of galvanized steel. It includes compact air handling units with cross plate heat excangers as heat recovery and a nominal air flow rate of 200-1200 m3/h per unit. No ground heat exchanger, ventilation of side rooms, cellars or car parks are included.;
UUID: 7f3ffa87-0e85-42ed-8d39-adb8b2a5d6ec
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2003. Process information partly from 2008. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7f3ffa87-0e85-42ed-8d39-adb8b2a5d6ec.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
